92186335997 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171957 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186335998 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171957 #edb/ref 1039 "Expressing the Relationship Between the Rows of Pascal's Triangle in Terms of Binomial Coefficients" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171957 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186171809 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171957 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "9c976b6a-4523-51e1-a243-27aa8937db25" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171958 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049341 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171958 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186172597 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171958 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186172598 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171958 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186247384 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171958 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186247385 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171958 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186247386 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171958 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186247387 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171958 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186247388 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171958 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186338775 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171958 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186338776 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171958 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186338777 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171958 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186338778 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171958 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186338779 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171958 #edb/ref 1039 "Calculating Binomial Coefficients Using the Formula" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171958 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186171810 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171958 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "e5c108c0-f32a-5725-af3b-c3e747da09f2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172193 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186172763 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172193 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186172764 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172193 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186172765 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172193 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186172766 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172193 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186172840 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172193 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172193 #edb/ref 1045 "Pascal's Triangle and the Binomial Coefficients" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172193 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186172765 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172193 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049243 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172193 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "5ec40baf-865b-5a44-991d-3e7fe88c0d58" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172763 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186172764 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172763 #edb/ref 1061 18724 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172763 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2865273f-2c72-526a-8ae4-5f9b2067a41a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172763 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186171956 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172764 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186172840 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172764 #edb/ref 1061 18731 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172764 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1189fea7-65d2-5d2d-87d5-800d8204673c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172764 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186171957 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172765 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186172763 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172765 #edb/ref 1061 18977 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172765 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "133af8ac-b2ce-5603-9334-ce3da1e8d068" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172765 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186173144 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172766 #edb/ref 1061 19269 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172766 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "0b7576cb-372f-5a6a-ad5b-4f0b958a39e3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172766 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186171958 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172840 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186172766 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172840 #edb/ref 1061 23007 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172840 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b2f96998-bbd7-586b-b0d8-4cdbe2c42034" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172840 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186173146 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173144 #edb/ref 1064 "Remember that when counting the rows and positions in Pascal's triangle, we always start counting from zero!\n\n- The top row of Pascal's triangle is row $0.$\n\n- The first position of each row (on the left) is position number $0.$\n\nWe can write a value in Pascal's triangle as $\\displaystyle{\\color{red}{a} \\choose {\\color{blue}b}},$ where the value is located in row $\\color{red}a$ and position ${\\color{blue}b}.$\nThis is known as a **binomial coefficient**.\nIn words, we say $\\displaystyle{\\color{red}{a} \\choose {\\color{blue}b}}$ as \"$\\color{red}{a}$ choose ${\\color{blue}b}$\".\n\nFor example, the value located in row $\\color{red}4$ and position $\\color{blue}2$ is highlighted below.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} &  &  &  &  & 1 \\\\  &  &  &  & 1 &  & 1 \\\\  &  &  & 1 &  & 2 &  & 1 \\\\  &  & 1 &  & 3 &  & 3 &  & 1 \\\\  & 1 &  & 4 &  & 6 &  & 4 &  & 1 \\\\ ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\displaystyle{{\\color{red}4} \\choose \\color{blue}{2}} = 6.$ Remember, we start counting from zero." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173144 #edb/ref 1065 3393 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173144 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "62d4b142-a86a-52c9-b45a-1153afedf865" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173144 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173146 #edb/ref 1064 "Suppose that we wanted to calculate the value of $\\displaystyle{30 \\choose 3}.$ If we were to use Pascal's triangle, we'd have to write out $31$ rows, which would take a long time. Thankfully, there is a formula for calculating binomial coefficients. \n\nThe binomial coefficient $\\displaystyle{n \\choose r}$ is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle{n \\choose r} = \\dfrac{n!}{(n-r)!\\,  r!}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173146 #edb/ref 1065 3893 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173146 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "b89d1a7e-10c1-5ec2-b745-c3c45e0d7814" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173146 #edb/ref 1067 "A Formula for the Binomial Coefficients" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186245535 #edb/ref 1080 "(\\frac{5}{3})" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186245535 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186245535 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "8b3b1495-fd4e-590e-abf2-f1d01bed44e4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186245807 #edb/ref 1080 "(\\frac{4}{3})" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186245807 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186245807 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a6d0e7ca-9cf6-56d2-bd14-35cdeb9caa81" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246060 #edb/ref 1080 "(\\frac{6}{5})" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246060 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246060 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c4a33636-8960-5f5f-8599-a5cf57881efe" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246113 #edb/ref 1080 "(\\frac{5}{5})" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246113 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246113 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "caa06872-b168-58f8-a4a8-ab8168991c78" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246157 #edb/ref 1080 "(\\frac{4}{4})" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246157 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246157 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ce63f89f-656b-512a-96b3-aa29379755eb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246939 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186245535 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246939 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186245807 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246939 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186246060 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246939 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186246113 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246939 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186246157 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246939 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246939 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246939 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186245535 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246939 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "dafab0b3-0ea9-52f1-b23d-e401a912ba3a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247383 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186246939 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247383 #edb/ref 1069 "q-113611" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247383 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247383 #edb/ref 1071 "Which expression is missing in the following equation?\n\n$$\n(\\frac{6}{4})=[]+(\\frac{5}{4})\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247383 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b7e46def-b53d-544e-a445-f2ab7d8b4fbc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247383 #edb/ref 1074 "To find $(\\frac{6}{4}),$ we need to find the number that is located in row $6$ and position $4$ of Pascal's triangle. \n\n**Important**: When counting the rows and positions in Pascal's triangle, we always start counting from zero! Remember:\n\n- The top row of Pascal's triangle is row $0.$\n\n- The first position of each row (the one of the left) is position number $0.$\n\nThe location of $(\\frac{6}{4})$ in Pascal's triangle is highlighted below.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} &  &  &  &  &  &  &  & (\\frac{0}{0}) \\\\  &  &  &  &  &  &  & (\\frac{1}{0}) &  & (\\frac{1}{1}) \\\\  &  &  &  &  &  & (\\frac{2}{0}) &  & (\\frac{2}{1}) &  & (\\frac{2}{2}) \\\\  &  &  &  &  & (\\frac{3}{0}) &  & (\\frac{3}{1}) &  & (\\frac{3}{2}) &  & (\\frac{3}{3}) \\\\  &  &  &  & (\\frac{4}{0}) &  & (\\frac{4}{1}) &  & (\\frac{4}{2}) &  & (\\frac{4}{3}) &  & (\\frac{4}{4}) \\\\  &  &  & (\\frac{5}{0}) &  & (\\frac{5}{1}) &  & (\\frac{5}{2}) &  & (\\frac{5}{3}) &  & (\\frac{5}{4}) &  & (\\frac{5}{5}) \\\\  &  & (\\frac{6}{0}) &  & (\\frac{6}{1}) &  & (\\frac{6}{2}) &  & (\\frac{6}{3}) &  & (\\frac{6}{4}) &  & (\\frac{6}{5}) &  & (\\frac{6}{6}) \\\\  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, $(\\frac{6}{4})$ is the sum of the two closest numbers located in the previous row. So,\n\n$$\n(\\frac{6}{4})=(\\frac{5}{3})+(\\frac{5}{4})\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expression is $(\\frac{5}{3}).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
